BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-178471@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260404T064357Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260410T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260410T183000
SUMMARY:Author Talk: "The Best Dog in the World" with Alice Hoffman
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 8 spots left\nSt
 atus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/178471
 \n\n5:00PM Reception\, 5:30PM Discussion\nFor anyone who has ever loved a 
 dog\, the bond needs little explanation. Join us for an intimate evening w
 ith bestselling author Alice Hoffman\, whose work so often explores the de
 pths of love\, connection\, and what it means to care deeply—for one ano
 ther and for the animals who share our lives.\n\nDrawing from her new essa
 y collection\, The Best Dog in the World: Essays on Love\, Hoffman reflec
 ts on the joy\, loyalty\, and quiet wisdom our canine companions bring. Fe
 aturing contributions from an extraordinary group of writers\, the collect
 ion is a heartfelt tribute to the dogs who leave lasting imprints on our l
 ives.\n\nThe conversation will be moderated by Mike Travis\, Chief Develo
 pment Officer of MSPCA-Angell\, one of the nation’s leading animal welf
 are and veterinary care organizations. Founded in 1868\, MSPCA-Angell has 
 long been at the forefront of animal protection and compassionate care—a
 n institution with which Hoffman shares a personal connection\, having ent
 rusted them with the care of her own dogs over the years.\n\nWarm\, though
 tful\, and deeply resonant\, this conversation offers a moving exploration
  of companionship\, empathy\, and the enduring bond between people and the
 ir animals.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only.
  Light bites and refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/178471
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
