SUMMARY:Author's Circle Book Club: "Impersonation" with Heidi Pitlor
LOCATION:The Terrace
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 3 spots left\nSt
 atus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/179449
 \n\nBookmark the date for a compelling conversation exploring Impersonatio
 n with Heidi Pitlor - a sharp\, satirical novel about ambition\, motherhoo
 d\, and the blurred boundaries between identity and performance.\n\nAllie 
 Lang is a professional ghostwriter and a perpetually broke single mother. 
 After years of navigating the cultural expectations placed on mothers\, an
 d the financial precarity of her work\, she has grown wary of the stories 
 she is asked to tell\, and the lives she is asked to inhabit.\n\nLana Breb
 an is a formidable lawyer\, economist\, and rising political figure prepar
 ing for a run for office. When her team commissions a memoir to soften her
  public image\, Allie is hired to ghostwrite the story of Lana’s life as
  a mother.\n\nAs personal pressures mount and Lana proves more exacting th
 an forthcoming\, the boundaries between subject and writer\, truth and per
 formance\, begin to blur. Allie is forced to reckon with how long she can 
 remain in the background of other people’s stories\, and what it will co
 st her to finally step into her own.\n\n*This event is complimentary and r
 eserved for members only. Light bites and refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/179449
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
